nodecode-bharatcode is a rewrite of thenabbu's thenabbu/bharatcode-hermes:

  https://github.com/thenabbu/bharatcode-hermes
  commit f4cc1d1f2977963173b23b9ac6a19c3ca8851050

  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Navya Gupta (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the provider profile itself — its OpenAI-compatible base
of https://bharatcode.ai/api/model/v1, its API-key auth and the key variable
it reads (BHARATCODE_API_KEY), its display name and description, its
sign-up page, its two fallback models, and its supports_vision=True claim —
as a Nodecode catalog row, a credential hook, and one bounded read of the
provider's own GET /models (kept, refreshed every ten minutes, and serving the
last good answer through a failure) so the picker offers the models the
account may actually use. Every row the picker offers is marked as taking
images, as the original declares of every model of this provider.

What was left out, and why: the original's provider aliases (bharat-code,
bharatcode-ai) have no place in Nodecode's catalog, which keys a provider by
one id. Its default_max_tokens of 32768 has no provider-level home in a
catalog row, so a turn's own ceiling stands. And the live catalog the
original's README promises is Hermes asking /models on its own; here the cell
makes that read itself, with the same shape, since Nodecode's catalog is
static otherwise.
